  (spec.md) requires the test to fail when a probe id has no map entry or a
  domain or kind is not valid. The fix embeds the harness path in the script
  text, the same pattern `callDomainCells` already uses.
- D2 confirmed, spec not ambiguous. Spec FR-3 requires an entry built from a
  revision 1 record with `E.labels: false` to omit `E.labels` from
  `domains.E.failed`. Test-strategy 5.3.1 requires a revision 1 Pi record and
  reads its history entry. The old seed wrote the revision 1 record with an
  OpenCode executor, so the history entry came from the revision 2 record,
  where `E.labels: false` correctly counts as a failure. The fix makes the
  arm-a revision 1 record a Pi record with `E.submits: false` and keeps the
  arm-b revision 2 record as OpenCode. The assertion now requires exactly
  `["E.submits"]`, which proves the entry source and the since rule.

